    description: "Author docs/adr/00XX-survey-rename.md capturing the rename decision: artifact filename moves from the current mix (CLI default `hypergumbo.results.json`, docs shorthand `hg.json`, test/dogfood `bm.json`, legacy `behavior_map.json`) to a single canonical name `survey.json`. Rationale: existing names lack one or more of [methodology, evidence, comprehensiveness, dignity]; survey captures all four and works as a verb. Document: (a) the chosen single canonical name, (b) the migration story (backward-compat window for old filenames), (c) the relationship to the v0.x stability commitment (the schema doesn't change; the filename does), (d) whether the verb `hypergumbo run` also moves to `hypergumbo survey` (separate decision; tracker item S9). Load-bearing decision document — must land before code changes."  # 4c17
